  "description": "A parametric TOILET PAPER HOLDER on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nSMALL, AND WORTH DRAWING ANYWAY. It is the object that turns a WC into a usable WC on a fit-out drawing, and the published \"Reach from the WC\" — 300 mm — is the figure that decides whether it is in the right place.\n\nTHE ROLL IS A RING seen edge-on: an ellipse whose radii are the roll's width across the bracket and its radius up the wall, extruded through the projection. That is the only way to draw a cylinder lying on its side in a language whose solid primitive is a swept quad.\n\nTHREE STYLES. Bracket projects from the wall; Recessed pulls the arm back into the wall face; Free-standing abandons the wall entirely for a post on a base, and moves the roll down to sit on it — one ternary on the arm's height, not a second object.",
